1
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:17,250
This is because I didn't take 
the time to listen to her.

2
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:21,080
Could she have... run away from home?

3
00:00:29,810 --> 00:00:30,850
Van?

4
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:45,420
"Must get medicine... from the Vankreift 
family... we must... the young lady."

5
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:50,230
I heard a voice saying that.

6
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:51,440
What did you say?!

7
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:53,900
Could it be...

8
00:00:56,530 --> 00:01:00,370
Was she mistakenly kidnapped instead of me?

9
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:08,000
Uncle, I-I'm sorry...

10
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:12,270
Ellen, it's not your fault.

11
00:01:13,230 --> 00:01:14,930
Please don't cry.

12
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:20,610
But... But because of
 the medicine I made, she...

13
00:01:21,990 --> 00:01:25,140
Your work has saved a great many lives.

14
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:28,150
The people who kidnapped 
Rafilia are the ones to blame.

15
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:30,770
Not you, Ellen.

16
00:01:36,610 --> 00:01:37,660
Your Grace.

17
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:38,470
What is it?

18
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:43,910
Before milady's disappearance, she received
 a letter from His Highness Gadiel.

19
00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:45,910
Why would he send her a letter?

20
00:01:46,290 --> 00:01:50,380
Prince Gadiel previously came
 to visit Lady Ellen.

21
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:52,620
Yes, I was informed of that.

22
00:01:53,060 --> 00:01:57,800
Ever since Rafilia and the prince met, 
they've been exchanging letters.

23
00:01:58,110 --> 00:02:01,010
Pardon me, but this is the letter.

24
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:06,020
It was left on her desk,
 so I assume she read it today.

25
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:13,180
Prince Gadiel has summoned Rafilia.

26
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:14,500
So the one who kidnapped her—

27
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:18,610
Wait! Are you saying the group after 
Ellen's medicine is the royal family?

28
00:02:19,090 --> 00:02:21,130
If His Highness has summoned her, 
that seems likely.

29
00:02:21,130 --> 00:02:22,220
Still...

30
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:26,700
She also could have been grabbed
 going to see His Highness.

31
00:02:27,060 --> 00:02:29,180
There is that possibility, yes.

32
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:31,810
We don't know why the prince
even summoned her.

33
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:32,790
Van.

34
00:02:33,430 --> 00:02:38,270
Could you hear them saying "the prince,"
 "young lady," and "medicine"?

35
00:02:38,270 --> 00:02:42,930
Yeah. Sounds like they're snooping around.

36
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:44,940
They're here?! In our domain?

37
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:46,120
Yes, they are.

38
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:47,730
Then perhaps it <i>was</i> His Highness...

39
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:49,410
Where? Where are they?!

40
00:02:49,410 --> 00:02:50,900
Take me to them right now!

41
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:32,060
THE KIDNAPPING INCIDENT

42
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:37,910
<i>Perhaps the spirits are involved after all.</i>

43
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:43,330
It seems no one knows the identity
 of the Healing Princess.

44
00:04:43,330 --> 00:04:44,430
Indeed.

45
00:04:45,690 --> 00:04:47,980
<i>If only we could uncover
the nature of her medicines.</i>

46
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:53,610
However, there are terms you must 
adhere to in your research, Hume.

47
00:04:54,330 --> 00:04:58,890
The Vankreifts are very special 
to the royal family, after all.

48
00:05:00,630 --> 00:05:04,080
<i>The conditions His Majesty 
set forth were to include the prince</i>

49
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:07,660
<i>on this journey and my research
 on the medicines... But why?</i>

50
00:05:08,270 --> 00:05:08,950
Gaddis.

51
00:05:09,430 --> 00:05:10,410
What is it?

52
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:14,500
Have you ever met the hero's daughter?

53
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:15,320
What?

54
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:18,880
Highness, please stand back!

55
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,460
I can protect myself!

56
00:05:24,110 --> 00:05:25,970
Give back my daughter.

57
00:05:26,230 --> 00:05:28,350
You're... What are you doing here?

58
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:32,720
Silence. You lured out my daughter 
to have her kidnapped, didn't you?!

59
00:05:34,610 --> 00:05:35,390
Ashute?

60
00:05:35,390 --> 00:05:36,640
Where is my daughter?!

61
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:38,060
Watch your mouth!

62
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:42,520
Get out of my way!

63
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:43,670
Wait, Uncle!

64
00:05:46,690 --> 00:05:47,860
Ellen...

65
00:05:48,430 --> 00:05:50,570
They're saying Rafilia isn't here.

66
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:51,580
What?

67
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:54,040
I confirmed it with the spirits,

68
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:56,540
so please calm down, Uncle.

69
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:58,500
<i>Just as I thought.</i>

70
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:03,210
She's not? Rafilia's... not here?

71
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:06,310
Ellen!

72
00:06:07,610 --> 00:06:08,680
I've wanted to see you.

73
00:06:12,350 --> 00:06:13,970
No... Don't come near me!

74
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:17,730
What?!

75
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:20,770
I ask that you not approach my daughter.

76
00:06:22,590 --> 00:06:24,320
Rovel Vankreift!

77
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:27,180
Did you forget what happened three years ago?

78
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:30,740
I haven't forgotten.
 That's why I want to apologize.

79
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:32,660
<i>Three years ago?</i>

80
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:33,740
<i>That's right!</i>

81
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:37,750
<i>That was when the royal family 
discovered they're cursed by the spirits.</i>

82
00:06:38,370 --> 00:06:41,850
Now then, let's hear it, shall we?

83
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:47,930
Prince Gadiel, why did you summon my daughter?

84
00:06:47,930 --> 00:06:48,970
What do you mean?

85
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:53,930
After receiving this, my daughter snuck out 
of the mansion and hasn't been seen since.

86
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:55,140
A letter?

87
00:06:55,140 --> 00:06:57,720
Don't play dumb with me!
You're the one who called for her!

88
00:06:57,980 --> 00:07:00,630
Cut the crap, Sauvel Vankreift!

89
00:07:00,630 --> 00:07:01,550
Vogel!

90
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:05,820
Duke Sauvel, please let me see that.

91
00:07:15,870 --> 00:07:19,460
It's true that Rafilia and I 
have been exchanging letters.

92
00:07:20,050 --> 00:07:22,290
However, I did not write this.

93
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:26,250
That's the royal crest! There's no 
talking your way around that.

94
00:07:26,530 --> 00:07:27,820
It is, yes.

95
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:30,360
Still, I swear I did not write this.

96
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,470
Please believe me.

97
00:07:32,690 --> 00:07:35,930
Then what brings you here?

98
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:38,970
Research.

99
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:44,020
Rumors say the Vankreift family possesses
 medicines effective against the epidemic.

100
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:45,080
Your Highness!

101
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:47,160
There's no point in hiding it.

102
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:52,260
The only way to prove that we didn't 
kidnap Rafilia is to speak up.

103
00:07:52,710 --> 00:07:54,820
You truly are the king's son.

104
00:07:55,230 --> 00:07:57,410
I'm glad to see you're quick on the uptake.

105
00:07:58,340 --> 00:08:01,590
We only meant to research the source 
and the effects of the medicine.

106
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:04,540
In fact, the king has been worried.

107
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:05,940
Worried?

108
00:08:06,510 --> 00:08:10,130
According to the rumors, 
your skilled apothecary is Ellen.

109
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:13,510
So before something happens to her,

110
00:08:13,510 --> 00:08:15,470
he ordered me to find out the truth.

111
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:19,930
<i>Why would Mr. Blackheart be worried 
about me? What is he scheming?</i>

112
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:23,390
But he'd never kidnap Rafilia to that end!

113
00:08:28,730 --> 00:08:31,360
Are you the spirit princess?

114
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:33,450
Huh? I'm...

115
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:35,550
And who might you be?

116
00:08:35,550 --> 00:08:37,990
I am Hume, a court healer.

117
00:08:38,610 --> 00:08:40,190
I see.

118
00:08:40,190 --> 00:08:45,290
I have a spirit friend named Ashute. 
It's very cute.

119
00:08:45,610 --> 00:08:47,500
<i>Even though he serves the royal family?</i>

120
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:50,300
You have a pact with a spirit?

121
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:53,460
Yep, we're best friends. Don't believe me?

122
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,270
Then I'll show you.

123
00:08:57,270 --> 00:09:01,110
But Your Highness, don't come 
near us no matter what, okay?

124
00:09:02,270 --> 00:09:03,710
Come on out, Ashute.

125
00:09:12,010 --> 00:09:14,530
Let me introduce you. Look, Ashute.

126
00:09:17,450 --> 00:09:19,410
Pwincess!

127
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:25,270
That's what I thought. 
You really are the spirit princess.

128
00:09:27,130 --> 00:09:31,910
I always had my suspicions that spirits were 
somehow involved with the medicines.

129
00:09:31,910 --> 00:09:33,650
Now it all makes sense.

130
00:09:35,410 --> 00:09:38,260
I assume that makes you 
the Healing Princess as well.

131
00:09:39,900 --> 00:09:44,130
Father, I believe it's about time
 that we tell them.

132
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:45,770
Ellen, are you serious?

133
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:50,350
Yes. Rumors of the medicines have 
already reached the royal capital.

134
00:09:54,390 --> 00:09:57,570
Nice to meet you. My name is Ellen.

135
00:09:57,570 --> 00:10:01,240
As you said, I am the spirit queen's daughter.

136
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:04,200
The spirit queen's daughter?

137
00:10:04,490 --> 00:10:08,540
Allow me to explain the effects 
of the medicines you're after.

138
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:09,750
Are you certain, Ellen?

139
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:13,880
Yes. The king already knows of them.

140
00:10:14,530 --> 00:10:17,510
It would be best for the 
royal family to manage them

141
00:10:17,510 --> 00:10:20,340
rather than have the 
Vankreifts monopolize them.

142
00:10:20,850 --> 00:10:24,930
Also, concerning His Majesty's worry for me...

143
00:10:24,930 --> 00:10:31,060
That's because he fears my father and I
leaving this world if I'm compromised.

144
00:10:32,060 --> 00:10:34,020
Things are just as the king wants.

145
00:10:34,850 --> 00:10:35,980
What do you mean?

146
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:42,680
Our current predicament with Rafilia
 works in His Majesty's favor.

147
00:10:43,070 --> 00:10:47,700
Now, if it turns out the royal family
had anything to do with the kidnapping...

148
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:50,670
You had best be prepared.

149
00:10:50,670 --> 00:10:52,670
I told you I don't know anything of it!

150
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:56,170
There's no way His Majesty 
would have told you.

151
00:10:56,530 --> 00:10:58,420
That's just the kind of man he is.

152
00:11:01,220 --> 00:11:03,550
Have I been used by my own father?

153
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:07,650
If we find Rafilia, it will prove
 your innocence beyond a doubt.

154
00:11:07,650 --> 00:11:10,480
So please help us with the search.

155
00:11:10,770 --> 00:11:12,440
You're asking the prince to help?

156
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:15,900
You have already failed your mission.

157
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:18,400
Do you want to report that to His Majesty?

158
00:11:19,450 --> 00:11:21,610
What choice do we have?

159
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:25,010
I'm certain he'd meet such failure 
with a disappointed sigh.

160
00:11:25,530 --> 00:11:32,150
But what if you could redeem 
your failure by finding Rafilia?

161
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:33,670
What do you mean?

162
00:11:33,670 --> 00:11:35,530
I'm offering a deal.

163
00:11:35,530 --> 00:11:39,380
If you help me, I'll give you the details, 
as well as a sample,

164
00:11:39,380 --> 00:11:41,470
of the medicines at once.

165
00:11:41,850 --> 00:11:45,190
It's what His Majesty wants, 
so if you take it to him,

166
00:11:45,190 --> 00:11:47,640
your mission will be a success.

167
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:49,980
Do we have your word?

168
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:52,470
I am the spirit queen's daughter.

169
00:11:52,470 --> 00:11:56,320
On my pride as the heir to the Primordial King...

170
00:11:56,870 --> 00:11:57,900
I swear it.

171
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:00,860
The Primordial King...

172
00:12:01,380 --> 00:12:06,020
However, only on the condition
that Rafilia is rescued safely.

173
00:12:07,150 --> 00:12:08,120
Understood.

174
00:12:09,250 --> 00:12:12,690
As her friend, I'm worried 
about Rafilia as well.

175
00:12:14,930 --> 00:12:16,740
Then we have a deal.

176
00:12:20,170 --> 00:12:23,880
I bet you'd need a decent number 
of men to kidnap a noble girl.

177
00:12:24,310 --> 00:12:27,420
Ellen, why are you asking for their help?

178
00:12:24,530 --> 00:12:29,490
Three at the very least, 
and they wouldn't be going on foot.

179
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:29,490
Rafilia's life is at stake.

180
00:12:29,490 --> 00:12:31,870
We can't afford to be stingy, Father.

181
00:12:31,870 --> 00:12:33,600
That's certainly true.

182
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:37,820
The culprits likely used
 a carriage to grab her,

183
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:40,250
then stashed it somewhere inconspicuous.

184
00:12:40,250 --> 00:12:40,820
Yeah.

185
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:42,930
A path that a carriage could use...

186
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:45,410
Where does this road here lead?

187
00:12:45,950 --> 00:12:49,450
A quarry that our ancestors 
used to use, I believe.

188
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:52,380
No one goes there anymore, though...

189
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,230
That's it!

190
00:12:54,630 --> 00:12:56,840
Let's gather intel using 
the power of the wind.

191
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:59,840
Van, could you search
 around this area from above?

192
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:01,650
I'm on it.

193
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:06,620
I'm counting on you.

194
00:13:10,150 --> 00:13:11,720
A high-ranking spirit...

195
00:13:12,110 --> 00:13:17,440
He's a great spirit. They're the only ones 
who can take human form, after all.

196
00:13:17,690 --> 00:13:21,650
Oh! You were using the power of the wind 
to blow away the disease, weren't you?

197
00:13:21,650 --> 00:13:24,110
You noticed that?

198
00:13:25,190 --> 00:13:28,670
I thought there must be a
 high-ranking wind spirit around, but...

199
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:32,830
I see. That's another way to use such power.

200
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:37,540
<i>This Hume boy.... He has a 
very high affinity with the spirits.</i>

201
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:42,410
Sauvel.

202
00:13:43,750 --> 00:13:45,490
Let us await the report first.

203
00:13:45,490 --> 00:13:47,930
Uncle, I'm sure it'll be fine.

204
00:13:48,380 --> 00:13:50,230
Yeah. I'm sorry.

205
00:13:50,230 --> 00:13:51,390
Thank you, Ellen.

206
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:56,350
If only we knew what she looked like,
 we could use the water mirror.

207
00:13:56,650 --> 00:13:58,380
True enough.

208
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:02,070
More like, if only <i>you</i> remembered 
what Rafilia looked like...

209
00:14:02,380 --> 00:14:05,530
Sorry. I'm drawing a blank.

210
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:09,420
Well, Father, I suppose you <i>do</i> avoid women.

211
00:14:15,970 --> 00:14:18,770
<i>Van, please hurry.</i>

212
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:32,370
Ellen.

213
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,650
Oh, sorry. Please don't run.

214
00:14:38,140 --> 00:14:40,040
I have one favor to ask.

215
00:14:42,190 --> 00:14:47,570
If we manage to find Rafilia safely, 
I ask that you hear me out.

216
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:58,250
I wonder if the day will come that you
 and the spirits ever forgive me.

217
00:15:03,270 --> 00:15:04,620
I'll be back.

218
00:15:16,390 --> 00:15:18,130
Okay. I will.

219
00:15:18,130 --> 00:15:18,840
Huh?

220
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:24,290
Ellen.

221
00:15:25,470 --> 00:15:29,020
The curse will activate, so you 
mustn't go near His Highness.

222
00:15:29,020 --> 00:15:30,320
I know that!

223
00:15:30,910 --> 00:15:34,140
Hey, Ellen. Why were you 
staring at the prince?

224
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:38,140
Oh, I found it strange that
 he was smiling so happily

225
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:42,580
when I merely agreed that I'd speak with him.

226
00:15:43,270 --> 00:15:48,710
I forgot. When it comes to yourself, 
you're absolutely clueless, Ellen.

227
00:15:49,050 --> 00:15:50,470
What is that supposed to mean?

228
00:15:50,470 --> 00:15:52,470
Just that you're Miss Clueless! That's all!

229
00:15:52,870 --> 00:15:53,730
Princess!

230
00:15:54,860 --> 00:15:56,140
Van! How did it go?

231
00:15:56,500 --> 00:16:00,600
As you thought, princess. There appear
 to be seven men and one young girl.

232
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:02,060
Well done!

233
00:16:02,370 --> 00:16:03,520
Let's go, Sauvel!

234
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:04,730
Right!

235
00:16:04,730 --> 00:16:06,560
Wait a minute! What about us?

236
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:08,590
Wait at my mansion.

237
00:16:10,570 --> 00:16:11,790
Kai, I leave the prince to you!

238
00:16:11,790 --> 00:16:13,180
What? But I'm...

239
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:14,030
Kai.

240
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:18,200
Are you ready?! Let's go!

241
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:21,290
<i>Please, be safe!</i>

242
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:32,260
How long do we gotta stay like this?

243
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:34,630
We were told to wait for
further instructions, 'member?

244
00:16:37,190 --> 00:16:37,760
Huh?

245
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:41,680
Th-The hell are you guys?!

246
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:44,420
Van, where is the girl?

247
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:45,900
In the cave up ahead.

248
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:47,810
Hey, what's going on?

249
00:16:46,730 --> 00:16:50,980
One, two, three, four, five, six...

250
00:16:49,290 --> 00:16:50,980
Hey! What's up?

251
00:16:51,330 --> 00:16:53,950
One's missing. Where's the last one?

252
00:16:54,310 --> 00:16:56,660
I can sense a man deep within the cave.

253
00:16:57,050 --> 00:16:59,740
Sauvel, I'll take care of things here.

254
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:01,510
You go get your daughter.

255
00:17:01,510 --> 00:17:02,520
Understood.

256
00:17:03,170 --> 00:17:05,420
Don't ya be whispering!

257
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:06,830
If ya got no business, then—

258
00:17:09,940 --> 00:17:11,310
Go, Sauvel!

259
00:17:11,310 --> 00:17:12,780
I owe you one, Brother!

260
00:17:13,130 --> 00:17:14,220
What?

261
00:17:14,990 --> 00:17:16,180
As if we'd let you pass!

262
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:17,390
Hey!

263
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:21,770
I'm your opponent.

264
00:17:21,770 --> 00:17:23,840
Who are these people?

265
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:27,850
They're probably some vigilante group
hired to rescue the brat.

266
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:32,860
You lot dared to meddle with something
 you absolutely shouldn't have.

267
00:17:34,070 --> 00:17:37,410
You'll pay for that in full.

268
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:42,420
Wait, Rovel!

269
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:48,370
Ori!

270
00:17:48,650 --> 00:17:50,090
Mother?!

271
00:17:50,490 --> 00:17:52,540
Wh-What the...?

272
00:17:52,540 --> 00:17:53,700
Who's that?

273
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,850
Why are you here?

274
00:17:56,190 --> 00:18:01,720
Because! My precious, precious 
little Ellen is working so hard...

275
00:18:02,050 --> 00:18:04,930
Of course I want to pitch in too.

276
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:07,640
I can, can't I?

277
00:18:08,930 --> 00:18:10,360
Of course you can.

278
00:18:11,540 --> 00:18:14,790
That's... Why is <i>she</i> here?

279
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:16,320
Hey, what's wrong?!

280
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:20,750
I-I saw her before during the Monster Tempest.

281
00:18:20,750 --> 00:18:22,530
What are you talking about?

282
00:18:23,110 --> 00:18:23,790
That...

283
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:27,790
That's... Spirit Queen Origin!

284
00:18:28,510 --> 00:18:35,070
Then that means... that guy is 
the hero who saved the world!

285
00:18:36,980 --> 00:18:39,870
It's been ages since we've
fought together, hasn't it, Rovel?

286
00:18:39,870 --> 00:18:40,680
Yeah.

287
00:18:40,930 --> 00:18:44,560
Since the Monster Tempest, I'd say.
Brings back memories.

288
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:45,800
Let us do our best.

289
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:46,790
Smooch!

290
00:18:49,010 --> 00:18:52,380
Now, let's show them what we got!

291
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:57,350
Our powers... together!

292
00:19:01,620 --> 00:19:03,020
<i>I've never seen this before. </i>

293
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:07,350
<i>So </i>this<i> is my parents' power?</i>

294
00:19:22,310 --> 00:19:25,560
Oh my! Did we get a little too carried away?

295
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:28,230
But I feel so much better now!

296
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:31,050
See you later, my sweet Ellen!

297
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,070
Rafilia...

298
00:19:43,470 --> 00:19:44,360
Rafilia?

299
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:50,190
Rafilia!

300
00:19:50,190 --> 00:19:51,860
Who the hell're you guys?

301
00:19:55,170 --> 00:19:56,930
What do you want?

302
00:19:57,710 --> 00:19:59,640
I came to take my daughter back.

303
00:19:59,950 --> 00:20:04,590
Your daughter? Parents weren't invited here.

304
00:20:05,230 --> 00:20:06,470
I'll leave Rafilia to you.

305
00:20:06,470 --> 00:20:07,130
Right!

306
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:11,910
Hey, hey! Don't go thinkin' 
you got the run of the place!

307
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:14,770
Father!

308
00:20:17,190 --> 00:20:20,490
What's wrong? Can't do nothin', huh?!

309
00:20:23,930 --> 00:20:27,990
Wha— Barehanded?!

310
00:20:33,550 --> 00:20:37,780
I can't move it! Who the hell are...

311
00:20:39,090 --> 00:20:46,140
I am the knight commander of the 
Tenbahl Kingdom, Sauvel Vankreift!

312
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:48,850
What? The knight commander?!

313
00:20:50,250 --> 00:20:51,770
Take this!

314
00:20:51,770 --> 00:20:52,520
Wait—

315
00:21:09,390 --> 00:21:10,690
Father!

316
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,860
Father!

317
00:21:13,860 --> 00:21:14,950
Rafilia!

318
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:17,690
Are you hurt? Are you all right?!

319
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:20,710
Father!

320
00:21:22,210 --> 00:21:25,630
I'm glad... I'm so glad.

321
00:21:27,210 --> 00:21:29,750
I'm sorry for everything, Rafilia.

322
00:21:30,100 --> 00:21:31,620
Father...

323
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:36,200
Let's go home.

324
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:37,220
Yeah.

325
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:46,170
Oh, Uncle!

326
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:49,910
How is Rafilia?

327
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:52,100
She's fine.

328
00:21:52,620 --> 00:21:54,290
She was probably tense this whole time.

329
00:21:54,950 --> 00:21:56,280
She fell asleep.

330
00:21:57,510 --> 00:22:00,870
Alberto, please hand these guys 
over to the guard.

331
00:22:01,190 --> 00:22:02,270
Understood.

332
00:22:03,370 --> 00:22:06,420
Brother, sorry for worrying you.

333
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:10,930
No need to thank me. 
I'm glad your daughter is safe.

334
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:12,460
Yes.

335
00:22:18,130 --> 00:22:19,550
Thank goodness.

336
00:22:21,170 --> 00:22:24,630
Translation: Yukari Murase-Louden

337
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:28,340
Editing: Riley Dalton

338
